=========================================================
COROUTINE CANCELLATION – PREREQUISITES (DIRECT POINTS)
=========================================================

1️⃣ REQUIRED TO CANCEL A COROUTINE

✔ It must have a Job reference
   - launch {} returns a Job
   - You need that Job to call cancel()

✔ The Job must be in ACTIVE state
   - You cannot cancel a completed coroutine
   - You cannot cancel an already cancelled coroutine

✔ The coroutine must be COOPERATIVE
   - Cancellation in Kotlin is cooperative (not forceful)

---------------------------------------------------------

2️⃣ WHAT MAKES A COROUTINE COOPERATIVE?

✔ It must reach a suspension point such as:
     - delay()
     - yield()
     - withContext()
     - await()
     - Any suspend function

OR

✔ It must manually check cancellation state:
     - isActive
     - ensureActive()

---------------------------------------------------------

3️⃣ IF THESE ARE NOT PRESENT

❌ Coroutine will NOT stop immediately
❌ It will continue execution until completion

---------------------------------------------------------

CORE RULE:

Cancellation works only if:

Job is ACTIVE
AND
Coroutine is COOPERATIVE
